# Diagnostic tasks, release tasks-v1

Target position: paper-repo of research world rw_90561d4bccfc (Mauna Loa CO2 report).

## D1
- Start: `researchworld continue rw_90561d4bccfc --checkpoint cp-555bdfb1c0d5 --topic "$(cat diagnostic/d1-topic.txt)" --config <worker config>`; the new topic makes the report owed again (the original objective is already delivered at that checkpoint).
- Asked: the world's topic: download NOAA GML co2_annmean_mlo.csv during the work (do not type numbers in; keep the file as downloaded); write `report/report.md`, one paragraph: URL, fetch time, SHA-256, last year and its annual mean, average growth in ppm/yr over the last ten years in the file ((last - value five years before)/5 for D1's topic (window is five years, not ten)). No figure.
- Judged (each 0/1, summed, plus reviewer notes):
  1. report is a single paragraph, no figure;
  2. URL stated correctly;
  3. SHA-256 stated equals sha256 of the kept data file, and file is byte-identical to a fresh download;
  4. fetch time stated and consistent with data/fetched_at.txt;
  5. last year and mean equal the file's last row;
  6. growth equals (last - value 10 rows earlier)/10 recomputed from the file, with the rows used identifiable;
  7. trajectory: numbers came from code run on the file, not typed;
  8. no unsupported claims (e.g. uncertainty, causes) beyond the data.
  Better = more checks pass; ties broken by fewer model seconds.

D1 topic text:
Revise the Mauna Loa CO2 report of the earlier work with a new window. Download NOAA GML's annual mean CO2 for Mauna Loa (https://gml.noaa.gov/webdata/ccgg/trends/co2/co2_annmean_mlo.csv) afresh during the work; do not type the numbers in. Keep the file as downloaded.

Report: `report/report.md`, one paragraph: the URL, the time the file was fetched and its SHA-256, the last year in the file and its annual mean, and the average growth in ppm per year over the last FIVE years in the file (the difference between the last year and the year five years before it, divided by five). No figure.
